STORY.scripture({"1 KĔPHA 2:24":{"t":"who Himself bore our sins in His body on the timber, so that we, having died to sins, might live unto righteousness – by whose stripes you were healed.","book":"1 KĔPHA"},"DANI'AL 2:44":{"t":"“And in the days of these sovereigns the Al of the shamayim shall set up a reign which shall never be destroyed, nor the reign pass on to other people – it crushes and puts to an end all these reigns and it shall stand forever.","book":"DANI'AL"},"DANI'AL 8:21":{"t":"“And the male goat is the sovereign of Greece and the large horn between its eyes is the first sovereign.","book":"DANI'AL"},"EZRA 1:1":{"t":"And in the first year of Koresh sovereign of Persia, that the Word of (YAHUAH) HWHY by the mouth of Yahrmeyah might be accomplished, (YAHUAH) HWHY stirred up the ruach of Koresh sovereign of Persia, to proclaim throughout all his reign and also in writing, saying,","book":"EZRA"},"GALATIANS 4:4":{"t":"But when the completion of the time came, Aluahim sent forth His Son, born of a woman, born under Torah,","book":"GALATIANS"},"LUKE 1:26":{"t":"And in the sixth month the mal'ak Gaḇri’al was sent by Aluahim to a city of Galil named Natsareth,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:27":{"t":"to a maiden engaged to a man whose name was Yosĕph, of the house of Dawiḏ. And the maiden’s name was Miryam.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:28":{"t":"And the mal'ak, coming to her, said, “Greetings, favoured one, the Master is with you. Baruk are you among women!”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:29":{"t":"But she was greatly disturbed at his word and wondered what kind of greeting this was.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:30-33":{"t":"And the mal'ak said to her, “Do not be afraid, Miryam, for you have found chen with Aluahim. “And see, you shall conceive in your womb and shall give birth to a Son and call His Name Yahusha. ”He shall be great and shall be called the Son of the Most High. And (YAHUAH) HWHY Aluahim shall give Him the throne of His father Dawiḏ. “And He shall reign over the house of Ya‛aqoḇ forever and there shall be no end to His reign.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:34":{"t":"And Miryam said to the mal'ak, “How shall this be, since I do not know a man?”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:35-37":{"t":"And the mal'ak answering, said to her, “The Ruach HaQadash shall come upon you and the power of the Most High shall overshadow you. And for that reason the Qadash (Set Apart One) born of you shall be called: Son of Aluahim. “And see, Alisheḇa your relative, she has also conceived a son in her old age. And this is now the sixth month to her who was called barren, because with Aluahim no matter shall be impossible.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 1:38":{"t":"And Miryam said, “See the female servant of (YAHUAH) HWHY! Let it be to me according to your word.” And the mal'ak went away from her.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:1":{"t":"And it came to be in those days that a decree went out from Caesar Augustus for all the world to be registered.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:10":{"t":"And the mal'ak said to them, “Do not be afraid, for look, I bring you the besorah of great joy which shall be to all people.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:11":{"t":"“Because there was born to you today in the city of Dawiḏ a Saviour, who is Mashiach, the Master.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:12":{"t":"“And this is the sign to you: You shall find a baby wrapped up, lying in a feeding trough.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:13":{"t":"And suddenly there was with the mal'ak a crowd of the heavenly host praising Aluahim and saying,","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:14":{"t":"“Esteem to Aluahim in the highest and on earth shalom among men with whom He is pleased!”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:15":{"t":"It came to be, when the mal'akim had gone away from them into the shamayim, that the shepherds said to each other, “Indeed, let us go to Bĕyth Leḥem and see this matter that has taken place, which the Master has made known to us.”","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:16":{"t":"And they came in haste and found Miryam and Yosĕph and the baby lying in a feeding trough.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:17":{"t":"And having seen, they made known the matter which was spoken to them concerning the child.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:18":{"t":"And all those who heard marvelled at what the shepherds said to them.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:19":{"t":"But Miryam kept all these matters, considering them in her heart.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:2-3":{"t":"This took place as a first registration while Quirinius was governing Syria. And all were going to be registered, each one to his own city.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:20":{"t":"And the shepherds returned, boasting and praising Aluahim for all they had heard and seen, as it was spoken to them.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:4-5":{"t":"And Yosĕph also went up from Galil, out of the city of Natsareth to Yahuḏah, to the city of Dawiḏ, which is called Bĕyth Leḥem, because he was of the house and lineage of Dawiḏ, to be registered with Miryam, who was engaged to him – being pregnant.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:7":{"t":"And she gave birth to her first-born Son and wrapped Him up and laid Him down in a feeding trough, because there was no room for them in a lodging place.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:8":{"t":"And in the same country there were shepherds living out in the fields, keeping watch over their flock by night.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 2:9":{"t":"And look, a mal'ak of (YAHUAH) HWHY stood before them and the esteem of (YAHUAH) HWHY shone around them and they were greatly afraid.","book":"LUKE"},"LUKE 4:18-21":{"t":"“The Ruach of (YAHUAH) HWHY is upon Me, because He has anointed Me to bring the Besorah to the poor. He has sent Me to heal the broken-hearted, to proclaim release to the captives and recovery of sight to the blind, to send away crushed ones with a release, to proclaim the acceptable year of (YAHUAH) HWHY.” And having rolled up the scroll, He gave it back to the attendant and sat down. And the eyes of all in the qahal were fixed upon Him. And He began to say to them, “Today this Scripture has been filled in your hearing.”","book":"LUKE"},"MATTITHYAHU 11:5":{"t":"“Blind receive sight and lame walk, lepers are cleansed and deaf hear, dead are raised up and poor are brought the Besorah.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 1:18":{"t":"But the birth of Yahusha Mashiach was as follows: After His mother Miryam was engaged to Yosĕph, before they came together, she was found to be pregnant from the Ruach HaQadash.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 1:19":{"t":"And Yosĕph her husband, being righteous and not wishing to make a show of her, had in mind to put her away secretly.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 1:20-21":{"t":"But while he thought about this, see, a mal'ak of (YAHUAH) HWHY appeared to him in a dream, saying, “Yosĕph, son of Dawiḏ, do not be afraid to take Miryam as your wife, for that which is in her was brought forth from the Ruach HaQadash. “She shall give birth to a Son and you shall call His Name Yahusha for He shall save His people from their sins. ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 1:22-23":{"t":"And all this came to be in order to fill what was spoken by (YAHUAH) HWHY through the naḇi, saying, “See, a maiden shall conceive and she shall give birth to a Son and they shall call His Name Immanu’al,” which translated, means, “Al with us.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 1:24":{"t":"And Yosĕph, awaking from his sleep, did as the mal'ak of (YAHUAH) HWHY commanded him and took his wife,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:1":{"t":"And Yahusha having been born in Bĕyth Leḥem of Yahuḏah in the days of Herodes the sovereign, see, Magi from the East came to Yahrushalayim,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:10":{"t":"And seeing the star, they rejoiced with exceedingly great joy.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:11":{"t":"And coming into the house, they saw the Child with Miryam His mother and fell down and did reverence to Him and opening their treasures, they presented to Him gifts of gold and frankincense and myrrh.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:12":{"t":"And having been warned in a dream that they should not return to Herodes, they departed for their own country by another way.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:13":{"t":"And when they had left, see, a mal'ak of (YAHUAH) HWHY appeared to Yosĕph in a dream, saying, “Arise, take the Child and His mother and flee to Mitsrayim and remain there until I bring you word, for Herodes is about to seek the Child to destroy Him.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:14-15":{"t":"And rising up, he took the Child and His mother by night and departed for Mitsrayim, and remained there until the death of Herodes, to fill what was spoken by (YAHUAH) HWHY through the naḇi, saying, “Out of Mitsrayim I have called My Son.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:2":{"t":"saying, “Where is He who has been born Sovereign of the Yahuḏim? For we saw His star in the East and have come to do reverence to Him.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:3-4":{"t":"And Herodes the sovereign, having heard, was troubled and all Yahrushalayim with him. And having gathered all the chief kohanim and scribes of the people together, he asked them where the Mashiach was to be born.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:5-6":{"t":"And they said to him, “In Bĕyth Leḥem of Yahuḏah, for thus it has been written by the naḇi, ‘But you, Bĕyth Leḥem, in the land of Yahuḏah, you are by no means least among the rulers of Yahuḏah, for out of you shall come a Ruler who shall shepherd My people Yasharal.’ ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:7":{"t":"Then Herodes, having called the Magi secretly, learned exactly from them what time the star appeared.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:8":{"t":"And having sent them to Bĕyth Leḥem, he said, “Go and search diligently for the Child and when you have found Him, bring back word to me, so that I too might go and do reverence to Him.”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 2:9":{"t":"And having heard the sovereign, they went. And see, the star which they had seen in the East went before them, until it came and stood over where the Child was.","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:16":{"t":"And having been immersed, Yahusha went up immediately from the water and see, the shamayim were opened and He saw the Ruach of Aluahim descending like a dove and coming upon Him,","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"MATTITHYAHU 3:3":{"t":"For this is he who was spoken of by the naḇi Yahshayahu, saying, “A voice of one crying in the wilderness, ‘Prepare the way of (YAHUAH) HWHY, make His paths straight.’ ”","book":"MATTITHYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 11:1-2":{"t":"And a Rod shall come forth from the stump of Yahshai and a Sprout from his roots shall bear fruit. The Ruach of (YAHUAH) HWHY shall rest upon Him – the Ruach of wisdom and understanding, the Ruach of counsel and might, the Ruach of knowledge and of the fear of (YAHUAH) HWHY,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 1:1":{"t":"The vision of Yahshayahu son of Amots, which he saw concerning Yahuḏah and Yahrushalayim in the days of Uzziyahu, Yotham, Aḥaz, Ḥizqiyahu – sovereigns of Yahuḏah.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 35:5-6":{"t":"Then the eyes of the blind shall be opened and the ears of the deaf be opened. Then the lame shall leap like a deer and the tongue of the dumb sing, because waters shall burst forth in the wilderness and streams in the desert.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 40:3":{"t":"The voice of one crying in the wilderness, “Prepare the way of (YAHUAH) HWHY; make straight in the desert a highway for our Aluahim.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 53:3-5":{"t":"despised and rejected by men, a man of pains and knowing sickness. And as one from whom the face is hidden, being despised and we did not consider Him. Truly, He has borne our sicknesses and carried our pains. Yet we reckoned Him stricken, smitten by Aluahim and afflicted. But He was pierced for our transgressions, He was crushed for our crookednesses. The chastisement for our shalom was upon Him and by His stripes we are healed.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 61:1-2":{"t":"The Ruach of the Master (YAHUAH) HWHY is upon Me, because (YAHUAH) HWHY has anointed Me to bring the besorah to the meek. He has sent Me to bind up the broken-hearted, to proclaim release to the captives and the opening of the prison to those who are bound, to proclaim the acceptable year of (YAHUAH) HWHY and the day of vengeance of our Aluahim, to comfort all who mourn,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 6:1":{"t":"In the year that Sovereign Uzziyahu died, I saw (YAHUAH) HWHY sitting on a throne, high and lifted up and the train of His robe filled the Hĕḵal.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:1":{"t":"And it came to be in the days of Aḥaz son of Yotham, son of Uzziyahu, sovereign of Yahuḏah, that Retsin sovereign of Aram and Peqaḥ son of Remalyahu, sovereign of Yasharal, went up to Yahrushalayim to fight against it, but could not prevail against it.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:10":{"t":"And (YAHUAH) HWHY spoke again to Aḥaz, saying,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:11":{"t":"“Ask a sign for yourself from (YAHUAH) HWHY your Aluahim; make deep the request or make it high.”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:12":{"t":"But Aḥaz said, “I do not ask nor try (YAHUAH) HWHY!”","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:13":{"t":"And he said, “Hear now, O house of Dawiḏ! Is it not enough that you weary men, that you weary my Aluahim also?","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:14":{"t":"“Therefore (YAHUAH) HWHY Himself gives you a sign: Look, the maiden conceives and gives birth to a Son and shall call His Name Immanu’al.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:2":{"t":"And it was reported to the house of Dawiḏ, saying, “Aram has set up camp in Ephrayim.” And his heart and the heart of his people were moved as the trees of the forest are moved with the ruach.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:3":{"t":"And (YAHUAH) HWHY said to Yahshayahu, “Go out now to meet Aḥaz, you and She’ar-Yashuḇ your son, at the end of the channel of the upper pool, on the highway of the Launderer’s Field,","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 7:4":{"t":"and say to him, ‘Take heed and be calm; do not fear or be faint-hearted for these two stubs of smoking fire brands, for the fierce displeasure of Retsin and Aram and the son of Remalyahu.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 8:16":{"t":"Bind up the witness and seal the Torah among my taught ones.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 8:17":{"t":"And I shall wait on (YAHUAH) HWHY, who hides His face from the house of Ya‛aqoḇ. And I shall look for Him.","book":"YASHAYAHU"},"YASHAYAHU 9:6-7":{"t":"For a Child shall be born unto us, a Son shall be given unto us and the rule is on His shoulder. And His Name is called Wonder, Counsellor, Strong Al, Father of Continuity, Prince of Shalom. Of the increase of His rule and shalom there is no end, upon the throne of Dawiḏ and over His reign, to establish it and sustain it with right-ruling and with righteousness from now on, even forever. The ardour of (YAHUAH) HWHY of hosts does this.","book":"YASHAYAHU"}});
